; chieftaincy","k":"Pirathon."},"6553":{"l":"פִּרְעָתוֹנִי","x":"Pirʻâthôwnîy","p":"pir-aw-tho-nee'","d":"a Pirathonite or inhabitant of Pirathon","r":"or ; patrial from H6552","k":"Pirathonite."},"6554":{"l":"פַּרְפַּר","x":"Parpar","p":"par-par'","d":"Parpar, a river of Syria","r":"probably from H6565 in the sense of rushing; rapid","k":"Pharpar."},"6555":{"l":"פָּרַץ","x":"pârats","p":"paw-rats'","d":"to break out (in many applications, direct and indirect, literal and figurative)","r":"a primitive root","k":"[idiom] abroad, (make a) breach, break (away, down, -er, forth, in, up), burst out, come (spread) abroad, compel, disperse, grow, increase, open, press, scatter, urge."},"6556":{"l":"פֶּרֶץ","x":"perets","p":"peh'-rets","d":"a break (literally or figuratively)","r":"from H6555lemma פּרַץ missing vowel, corrected to פָּרַץ","k":"breach, breaking forth (in), [idiom] forth, gap."},"6557":{"l":"פֶּרֶץ","x":"Perets","p":"peh'-rets","d":"Perets, the name of two Israelites","r":"the same as H6556","k":"Perez, Pharez."},"6558":{"l":"פַּרְצִי","x":"Partsîy","p":"par-tsee'","d":"a Partsite (collectively) or descendants of Perets","r":"patronymically from H6557","k":"Pharzites."},"6559":{"l":"פְּרָצִים","x":"pᵉrâtsîym","p":"per-aw-tseem'","d":"Peratsim, a mountain in Palestine","r":"plural of H6556; breaks","k":"Perazim."},"6560":{"l":"פֶּרֶץ עֻזָּא","x":"Perets ʻUzzâʼ","p":"peh'-rets ooz-zaw'","d":"Perets-Uzza, a place in Palestine","r":"from H6556 and H5798; break of Uzza","k":"Perezuzza."},"6561":{"l":"פָּרַק","x":"pâraq","p":"paw-rak'","d":"to break off or crunch; figuratively, to deliver","r":"a primitive root","k":"break (off), deliver, redeem, rend (in pieces), tear in pieces."},"6562":{"l":"פְּרַק","x":"pᵉraq","p":"per-ak'","d":"to discontinue","r":"(Aramaic) corresponding to H6561","k":"break off."},"6563":{"l":"פֶּרֶק","x":"pereq","p":"peh'-rek","d":"rapine; also a fork (in roads)","r":"from H6561","k":"crossway, robbery."},"6564":{"l":"פָּרָק","x":"pârâq","p